<!-- @after Common Misconceptions :: check -->
**Which mechanism?** Decide before opening each answer.

<details><summary>A chat message that must appear within seconds while the phone sleeps.</summary>

A high-priority FCM message that results in a user-visible notification. Using high priority without notifying the user risks being downgraded.
</details>

<details><summary>A nightly backup of the user's photos.</summary>

WorkManager with constraints (unmetered network, charging). It runs in a maintenance window or when the constraints next hold.
</details>

<details><summary>Testing why a daily sync never runs in production.</summary>

Put the app in the bucket real users are in (`adb shell am set-standby-bucket <package> rare`) and force idle to exercise Doze, instead of testing only while the screen is on and the phone is charging.
</details>
